# Keep the build context lean and never ship secrets or local data into the image.
# The Dockerfile copies backend/ and frontend/ explicitly; this excludes the cruft.

# Python. Patterns are matched relative to the build-context root and do NOT recurse for a
# bare `dir/`, so nested paths (e.g. backend/.venv) must be globbed explicitly — that venv is
# ~270MB / ~9.8k files and was the entire build-context bloat before these **/ globs.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest-cache/
**/.pytest-run-cache/
**/.pytest-tmp/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.venv/
.venv/

# Secrets and local env — provided as Fly secrets/build-args, never baked in. MUST use **/
# so NESTED env files are excluded too: a root-anchored `.env.*` does NOT match
# frontend/.env.local, which leaked VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 into the prod
# bundle and sent prod's API calls (incl. login) to localhost. (Same nested-path trap as .venv.)
**/.env
**/.env.*
.env
.env.*
backend/secrets/
backend/config/initial-admins.txt

# Databases and applicant data (PII) — the volume provides the live DB; never copy snapshots.
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
backend/data/
**/exports/
**/ai-traces/

# Frontend — node_modules is reinstalled in the build stage; dist is rebuilt there.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS, tooling, docs not needed at runtime
.git/
.github/
docs/
test-data/
*.md
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.claude/
